  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1246 PM MDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nMain impact is the return of extreme heat with heat advisories\nin effect for a good portion of southeast Idaho through \nSaturday. High temperatures approaching 100 in many areas this \nafternoon as well as Saturday afternoon with most areas mid to \nupper 90s in the advisory area. Still have some wildfire smoke \nin the region in and out to varying degrees with an air quality \nalert in Custer County. Forecast grids have dry conditions with \nslight cooling into the middle of next week with a slight chance\nof showers and thunderstorms returning next Thursday and Friday\nmainly in the southeast mountains. Winds not expected to be \noverly strong through the period with some high elevation gusts \nupwards of 25 mph Tomorrow and Sunday.",
